  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.5$ | $0.05$ | $0.55$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ | $0.45$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.65$ | $0.35$ | $1$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=0.45\\,\\text{E}[Y]=0.35,\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.4975,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.4770,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
